description: Laravel backend conventions (controllers, Form Requests, policies, actions, resources, tests)
globs: app/**, routes/**, config/**, bootstrap/app.php, database/**, tests/Feature/**, tests/Unit/**, tests/Concerns/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Follow "Backend conventions", "API contract" and "Tests" in @AGENTS.md.
The reference implementation is @app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/ProductController.php
with @app/Http/Requests/Products/ProductRequest.php and
@app/Policies/ProductPolicy.php.

Checklist for a backend change:

- Validation and authorization in a Form Request; policy linked with
  `#[UsePolicy]`; multi-step writes in `app/Actions/`; responses through
  `ApiResponse::success()` and a JsonResource.
- `UserController` checks authorization before it looks up an account; keep
  that order.
- Any `/api` change also updates @docs/api/openapi.yaml and, for response
  fields, `tests/Feature/Api/ResponseFieldsTest.php`.
- Migrations and seeders: see @database/AGENTS.md.
- Run `docker compose exec -T app composer lint`, `composer analyse` and
  `php artisan test` in the `app` container. No PHPStan baseline or ignores.
